%% DM26-0670

%% The whole bootstrap of a Polar cluster from the sandbox-local target, in three phases.
%% This is the code in infra/ (traced in docs/architecture/cluster-bootstrap.md), run end to end on a podman
%% dev node on 2026-10-19, and from the dev pod on 2026-10-21 with the registry and the deployment git server in the cluster.
%% A target that does not set gitops: true applies its layers itself. Shaded: designed, not built (policy-enforcement.md).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Op as Operator
    participant Up as infra/up.nu
    participant Infra as In the cluster, before Polar<br/>registry (polar-registry)<br/>deployment git server (polar-deploy)
    participant K as Kubernetes API
    participant Flux as Flux controllers
    participant W as Polar workloads

    Op->>Up: nu infra/up.nu sandbox-local --user U --email E

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Op,W: PHASE 1 - before Flux. up.nu does what cannot be GitOps
    Up->>Infra: apply the registry (and the storage it needs), forward to it
    Up->>Infra: every image the target runs, before the render: copied (--import-from) or built (--dev)
    Up->>K: ask each agent's image for its scaffold, as a pod in a scratch namespace (cached by digest)
    Up->>Up: render the manifests (infra/render.nu), the registry the nodes use resolved once
    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Up->>Up: DESIGNED: the render writes each workload's declared topics into the issuance floors
    end
    Up->>K: apply namespaces, make the cluster CA, create the secrets (polar-admin-grant, secrets.nu)
    Up->>Infra: apply the deployment git server with its own PKI, re-seeded from mirror.git (deploy-repo.nu ensure)
    Up->>Infra: commit the layers there, signed with the pipeline certificate (deploy-repo.nu publish)
    Up->>K: install Flux after checking the head is signed, give it the repo's address and certificate
    end

    rect rgb(215, 227, 190)
    Note over Op,W: PHASE 2 - Flux. Layers are reconciled in order
    Flux->>Infra: pull the deployment repo over mTLS, by its Service
    Flux->>K: apply platform, cert-issuer, data, cassini, identity, agents,<br/>each after the one before is healthy
    K->>W: pods start and get their certificates
    Up->>K: wait until every layer reports Ready at the published commit (flux.nu wait)
    end

    rect rgb(204, 220, 232)
    Note over Op,W: PHASE 3 - after Flux. up.nu does what needs running workloads
    Up->>W: wait for the core services, port-forwards, then the admin flow (accounts and certificates)
    Up->>Infra: record the first admin as the git server's administrator, publish again, Flux restarts it
    Up->>W: sign and push the first policy to the schedules repository
    Up->>Op: ask to close the browser, import the certificate, check Neo4j
    Up->>Op: report that the target is up
    end
